{
  "_rotation_hold": "🔴 READ THIS FIRST — IT IS WHY THIS KEY LEADS THE RECORD. DO NOT ACT ON `_how_to_clear_the_red` BELOW WHILE THIS KEY IS PRESENT. Its fourth step — update detector_sha256, scanned_ref_sha, scan_fingerprint, the counts and real_findings — is the one thing the postgres-rotation hold refuses. The re-scan and triage are ALREADY DONE, on branch wt-maya-4f0ced13 at 034e44ac, held unmerged until Rick rotates the credential. The red is the only branch-level signal that the credential work is unfinished; greening it changes the signal, not the risk. WHY THIS KEY EXISTS RATHER THAN AN EDIT TO THE RECIPE: the recipe is the record of what the then-owner said to do, and rewriting a recorded string to fix a display destroys evidence (Mr Radio's ruling, 2026-08-30). Adding a key is annotation, not rewriting. It sits FIRST rather than beside the recipe (Krishna, reviewing 01516300) because a reader acts on the first instruction they find — which is the exact defect this whole change exists to fix, and it applied to the fix. The test's gate suppresses the recipe where it is PRINTED, but a human opening this file directly is reached by no gate at all — this key is what reaches them. REMOVE IT WHEN THE CREDENTIAL IS ROTATED, in the same change that flips ROTATION_HOLD_ACTIVE.",
  "_why": "A pre-commit gate only ever sees ADDED lines, so it is structurally blind to what is already in the tree. The only thing that finds an OLD secret is a full re-scan, and the moment a full re-scan pays is when the detector improves — on 2026-08-17 a word-boundary fix made every SCREAMING_SNAKE secret visible for the first time, including two passwords that had sat at the public tip. A weekly cadence would have sat on them for up to six more days. So this file pins the detector to the last full scan run with it: change src/scripts/secret_scan.py and test_secret_scan.py goes red until somebody re-scans and records the result here.",
  "_how_to_clear_the_red": [
    "python3 src/scripts/secret_scan.py ref origin/main   # and 'history' if the question is the whole repo",
    "python3 src/scripts/secret_scan.py ref <the working branch>   # what we commit to, which origin/main is not",
    "triage the output — it is masked; a raw candidate count is not a finding",
    "update detector_sha256, scanned_ref_sha, scan_fingerprint, the counts and real_findings",
    "for a NEW branch finding: triage it, then add its masked row to branch_accepted with a note",
    "record the triage on the sweep row, not only here"
  ],
