  "_why_two_refs": "origin/main answers 'what can a stranger read'. It is not what we commit to: measured 2026-08-17, the working branch was 645 commits and two weeks ahead of it, so a credential committed today was seen by nothing — the gate reads only ADDED lines and is not installed, and the full scan read a ref nobody had pushed to in two weeks. The branch arm below closes that. It pins an ACCEPTED SET rather than a whole-ref fingerprint, because the branch moves many times a day and a fingerprint over it would be red permanently: a new finding is red, an ordinary commit is not.",
